  "notes": [
    "Table 3 covers the 1996 Acura SLX (badge-engineered Isuzu Trooper) and 1996 Trooper; Table 4 the 1994 Trooper.",
    "SSF = track width / (2 * CG height); the report notes the measured track widths differed between subject vehicles, so equal CG heights can give different SSF.",
    "The two CarT rows do not publish inertia columns; they are kept for CG height/SSF only.",
    "No modern sports-car inertia measurements were found under a public-domain or permissive licence; that gap is documented, not filled with estimates."
  ],
